# Every path the fork changes in Compose's source at the Windows pin, and the content it
# has there.
#
# The twin of compose-fork.changes, for MINGW_REVISION in build-compose.sh rather than
# REVISION: the same upstream base (JetBrains release/1.11, 73ac849), and on top of what the
# other pin holds, mingwX64 in every Compose UI module, skiko read from the local Maven
# repository first, and the skiko build for mingwX64 under extended/skiko.
# scripts/tests/compose-fork.test.sh reads the pinned commit's tree and checks every line.
#
# Format: the git blob hash the path must hold, or `-` where the path must be absent,
# then the path. Moving the pin means regenerating this from the new commit, and deciding,
# path by path, that each change is still there:
#
#   git diff --raw --no-renames --no-abbrev <upstream base> <pinned commit> |
#       awk '{ print ($5 == "D" ? "-" : $4), $6 }'
